<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-17 bug fix). Account.Record_Type_Is_Immutable
        (AND(NOT(ISNEW()), ISCHANGED(RecordTypeId))) blocks EVERY post-creation change to
        Account.RecordTypeId, including the one LeadConvertService.stampConvertedPartyRecordTypes
        makes on purpose: standard Database.convertLead does not map record types onto the
        Account it creates (see that method's header, LeadConvertService.cls), so conversion
        follow-up UPDATEs the converted Account to Broker_Firm. That UPDATE trips the same rule
        the IR-segregation change built to stop a record type being changed AFTER creation - the
        rule cannot tell "the deliberate one-time conversion stamp" apart from "someone
        reparenting an Account across the sharing boundary later," because both are
        ISCHANGED(RecordTypeId) on an existing row. Database.update(..., false) then swallows the
        failure silently, so RecordTypeId stayed null and
        LeadConvertServiceTest.conversionStampsBrokerRecordTypesOnContactAndAccount failed on
        "Actual: null" - not a permission-set provisioning gap (LeadConvertService.cls's own
        FIX ROUND 1 comment mis-diagnosed it that way; corrected in the same change that added
        this permission).

        The validation rule's own comment prescribes the fix: "If an exemption is ever needed,
        add a custom permission and gate on $Permission - never widen the rule itself." This is
        that custom permission, and it is scoped as narrowly as a $Permission gate can be scoped:
        it is granted ONLY to the two permission sets that cover every principal that actually
        reaches this UPDATE (traced via the call path, not assumed):

          1. Lead_Stage_Actions_Access - the permission set this repo already uses as the sole
             gate for "who may convert a Lead" (it carries the ConvertLeads user permission and
             is documented "Assign to reps who advance/convert Leads from the Lead record page").
             LeadConvertTrigger fires after Lead update; conversion is a USER-INITIATED action
             (see LeadConvertService.recordTypeId's header), so the real-world population that
             ever triggers stampConvertedPartyRecordTypes is exactly this permission set's
             holders.
          2. DPEG_Admin_Access - measured live against usman-dpeg (2026-08-17): the principal
             Apex tests and ad hoc admin conversions run as
             (usman.khan.dpeg@avanzasolutions.com) holds DPEG_Admin_Access but NOT
             Lead_Stage_Actions_Access. Modify All Data does not confer a custom-permission grant
             (see Acquisition_Deal_Driver.permissionset-meta.xml's identical note), so without
             this grant conversionStampsBrokerRecordTypesOnContactAndAccount would still fail
             for that principal even after the validation-rule change. Granting it here is
             consistent with the rule's own comment that admins are intended to be out of scope.

        ⚠ THIS IS NOT A GENERAL RECORD-TYPE-CHANGE BYPASS. Because $Permission gates by WHO the
        running user is, not by WHICH CODE PATH is running, any holder of either permission set
        above could in principle also change an existing Account's RecordTypeId by hand (Data
        Loader, UI edit) while this permission is active - that is the accepted, understood
        tradeoff of the $Permission mechanism the rule's own comment calls for, not a design
        oversight. Do not grant this permission set membership to any other permission set,
        profile, or persona without re-reading this note; the whole point of scoping it to
        exactly these two sets is that both populations are already the ones this UPDATE is
        meant to run for.
    -->
    <label>Lead Convert Account Record Type Stamp</label>
    <description>Exempts Account.Record_Type_Is_Immutable for LeadConvertService's post-conversion Broker_Firm stamp. Granted only via Lead_Stage_Actions_Access and DPEG_Admin_Access - see the in-file comment.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
